{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvtDJwpFpXGuwvLk9vjv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the text edits."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":315,"cache_read_input_tokens":65357,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":315},"output_tokens":29,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3ebd735c-ffc1-4510-b0aa-9e4a095cb3e8","uuid":"0299a21f-014c-46f5-a1c5-c49c02554ede","timestamp":"2026-11-11T09:12:59.532Z","request_id":"req_011CgvtDJMrF9Ma4imFiRbeh"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvtDJwpFpXGuwvLk9vjv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RTWWynB7CNe4KKEWcLVcit","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\nt=open('paper.tex').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global t\n    assert t.count(a)==1,a\n    t=t.replace(a,b)\nrep(r\"converts each model's score vector into a rank \\citep{Hendrycks2020MeasuringMM,Liang2022HolisticEO,Wang2019SuperGLUEAS}. Rankings influence adoption, publication and funding, so developers have an incentive to act on them.\",\n r\"converts each model's score vector into a rank \\citep{Hendrycks2020MeasuringMM,Liang2022HolisticEO}. Rankings influence adoption, publication and funding, so developers have an incentive to act on them, which is the familiar pattern in which a metric used as a target ceases to measure what it was meant to measure \\citep{Thomas2020RelianceOM}.\")\nrep(r\"Broad suites such as MMLU, BIG-bench and its hard subset, HELM and SuperGLUE summarize models by averaging over many sub-tasks \\citep{Hendrycks2020MeasuringMM,Srivastava2022BeyondTI,Suzgun2022ChallengingBT,Liang2022HolisticEO,Wang2019SuperGLUEAS}. The Open LLM Leaderboard aggregates six benchmarks \\citep{\",\n r\"Broad suites such as MMLU, its hard BIG-bench subset and HELM summarize models by averaging over many sub-tasks \\citep{Hendrycks2020MeasuringMM,Suzgun2022ChallengingBT,Liang2022HolisticEO}. The Open LLM Leaderboard \\citep{OpenLLMLeaderboardContents2025}, whose public snapshot supplies our held-out boards, aggregates six benchmarks \\citep{\")\nrep(r\"how little must change for a chosen candidate to win under a voting rule \\citep{Bartholdi1989TheCD,Faliszewski2006HowHI,Xia2012ComputingTM,Conitzer2016BarriersTM}. Complexity results depend on the rule, on the number of candidates, and on tie-breaking \\citep{Obraztsova2011TiesMC,Yang2014ElectionAW,Dey2014KernelizationCO}. Our problem is a continuous variant:\",\n r\"how little must change for a chosen candidate to win under a voting rule \\citep{Bartholdi1989TheCD,Faliszewski2006HowHI,Xia2012ComputingTM,Conitzer2016BarriersTM}. The closest discrete analogues price the intervention: bribery models give each voter a price for changing their vote \\citep{Faliszewski2006HowHI}, and swap bribery charges for each exchange of adjacent candidates in a voter's ranking \\citep{Elkind2009SwapB}. Complexity results depend on the rule and on tie-breaking; for example, Copeland voting has been studied for its resistance to bribery and control \\citep{Faliszewski2009LlullAC}, and tie-breaking conventions change manipulation complexity \\citep{Obraztsova2011TiesMC}. We cite these results as context only: we do not prove hardness for the planner's problems and do not claim that the planner's heuristics inherit any of these guarantees. Our problem is a continuous variant:\")\nopen('paper.tex','w').write(t)\nE\ngrep -n \"Wang2019\\|Srivastava\\|SuperGLUE\\|Dey\\|Yang2014\" paper.tex; sed -n 136p paper.tex | cut -c1-900"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":315,"cache_read_input_tokens":65357,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":315},"output_tokens":29,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3ebd735c-ffc1-4510-b0aa-9e4a095cb3e8","uuid":"852e2d26-174a-4a05-9f47-bf7087d61f01","timestamp":"2026-11-11T09:13:06.508Z","request_id":"req_011CgvtDJMrF9Ma4imFiRbeh"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RTWWynB7CNe4KKEWcLVcit","type":"tool_result","content":"\\paragraph{Data and splits.} Development uses the 57 HELM MMLU v1.13.0 subject columns as tasks. The held-out evaluation uses two boards built from the Open LLM Leaderboard snapshots: a six-benchmark board from the \\texttt{contents} table and a sub-task-level board from the \\texttt{results} files for the same model pool, each restricted to the top $\\min(N,200)$ models. The evaluator verifies snapshot checksums and checks that the held-out boards are disjoint from the development data. Development seeds are 11 and 12; held-out seeds are 9001 and 9002.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3ebd735c-ffc1-4510-b0aa-9e4a095cb3e8","uuid":"5c258903-224a-406a-a222-0bc669b308ed","timestamp":"2026-11-11T09:13:06.599Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\\paragraph{Data and splits.} Development uses the 57 HELM MMLU v1.13.0 subject columns as tasks. The held-out evaluation uses two boards built from the Open LLM Leaderboard snapshots: a six-benchmark board from the \\texttt{contents} table and a sub-task-level board from the \\texttt{results} files for the same model pool, each restricted to the top $\\min(N,200)$ models. The evaluator verifies snapshot checksums and checks that the held-out boards are disjoint from the development data. Development seeds are 11 and 12; held-out seeds are 9001 and 9002.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
